Z||000003||LZeitgeist||08-27-2001||02:00 PM||||Red is way overdone. I swear I see six red Fieros for each one of all the other colors put together. <P>I'd shoot for the gunmetal grey metallic... sounds *really* nice.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
Z||000004||Voytek||08-27-2001||03:18 PM||||Well, it depends on a few things.<BR>1.  Type of rims?  I don't have a suggestion here - you'll have to think on what goes good with your rims.  The choices you presented will go with most rims.<BR>2.  Do you want to stand out, i.e. turn heads or do you prefer less attention?  Mine is yellow and it turns heads ALL the time.  If I travel behind or in front of another GT fastback, mine is mostly the only one that gets the looks.<P>Having said that, I wouldn't go with black.  I don't mind it at all but it's too plain.<P>My second choice after yellow would be gun metal gray.<P>My third choice (and a really close one to the gray) would be the red.<P>Depending on the yellow, in the last 3 years since I had my car painted, I've only had one person complain.  Virtually everyone else is impressed - it really brings out the exotic curves of the Fiero.  I also couldn't decide on the color - sure glad I picked this one.<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
